/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate31_vp_monoethanolamine -- the vapour pressure of monoethanolamine, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 step 2).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  monoethanolamine`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION, committed
  before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1016/j.fluid.2015.06.045      38 pts  273.65-303.16 K  Ruzicka; Fulem; Mahnel; Cervinka
      10.1021/je800530u                26 pts  283.15-363.15 K  Belabbaci; Razzouk; Mokbel; Jose et al.
      10.1021/je800290k                16 pts  357.46-435.61 K  Kim; Svendsen; Borresen
      10.1021/je049761y                13 pts  279-324.5 K  Kapteina; Slovik; Verevkin; Heintz
      10.1021/je101259r                 7 pts  358.6-441.9 K  Klepacova; Huttenhuis; Derks; Versteeg
      10.1021/je400885z                 6 pts  373.15-423.15 K  McDougal; Jasperson; Wilson
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1021/je3002078: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je7001336: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1016/j.fluid.2015.06.045 (38 pts, 273.65-303.16 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1021/je800530u (26 pts,
  283.15-363.15 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 5.4 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 26 points (0.773 to 12 %, mean 5.314 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 444.15 K lies OUTSIDE the measured span 273.65-363.15 K: the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within 2 K of it, or the fit is NOT promoted (an extrapolation that misses the record's own boiling point).

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 6.766025 - 2807.2440/(T + -17.4236),
  in-sample R2 0.999993 over 38 points, 273.65-303.16 K. HELD OUT: 26
  points, AAD 2.8176 % against the band 5.4 % -> validated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 432.68 K. NOT PROMOTED: validated,
  but the fitted Antoine's normal boiling point 432.68 K misses the
  record's Tb 444.15 K by -11.47 K, outside the declared 2 K -- an
  extrapolation that contradicts the record; the record keeps
  AmbroseWalton
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  monoethanolamine;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/monoethanolamine-vapourPressure-j.fluid.2015.06.045.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.fluid.2015.06.045"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/monoethanolamine-vapourPressure-je800530u.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je800530u"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  5.4 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 26 points (0.773 to 12 %, mean 5.314 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
